// nothing moves (measured: suite green with these notes, 10 snapshots red without).
//
// ✔ VERIFIED TO GUARD, not assumed to (session 190) -- BUT THE HEADER'S "Guards the
// LayoutEngine post-pass that shifts articulations past a shared-side fingering" IS
// POINTING THE WRONG WAY, and is left standing above only because deleting it would
// shift this book's offsets and re-base its snapshot (a user's call, not this note's).
// MEASURED: the code does the opposite direction. Every fingering flushes AFTER all of
// its note's scripts are placed (ArticulationEngraver's final FlushFingerings at
// int.MaxValue), and that flush lifts the DIGIT clear of the scripts already there --
// nothing ever shifts an articulation past a fingering. Poisoning the two sites the
// header names (the early flush; adding the digit to supportScripts) moved 0 of 219
// fixtures. Poisoning the digit's own clearance (move := 0) moved exactly this book.
// ⚠️ AND IT IS THE ONLY OBSERVER: of the 566 git-tracked .lys this is the one book that
// reaches that flush with a non-empty support chain. Delete it and the lift is unwatched.
// ⚠️ The EARLY flush is not dead, only unwatched HERE: 5 tracked books reach it
// (audit/lpreg/{obs-probe,perf-fingstack1k,scriptstack1,slurscript-obs},
// audit/lp-regression/lys/script-stack-order1) and none of them is a fixture.
